Cliff Chen (chen@whatever.cs.jhu.edu) wrote:
: >>  My friends and I love NH3.1, great job! Only one tiny desire remains..
: >>A networked, multi-player version where you and all your friends can connect
: >>and go at it together or against each other at the same time.

[other thoughts on multi-player hack deleted]

Another problem with it is that the system would have to be real-time.
So if I was standing still in a room, someone would be able to come up
and kill me.  If you didn't allow that, everyone would have to wait for
everyone else to move.

Killing off other players would be very easy once you found good weapons.
Hell, just a wand of fire would be enough.

As far as only having one artifact: you just create more different artifacts.

Personally I don't think nethack quite fits into the multi-player type of
game.  You really couldn't set a goal for the game because someone else
might screw you up taking all the necessary items.

One feature that would be cool:  After a character ascends to Demi-god
hood, have the game keep that around like a bones character, except it
would be a computer controlled live one.  The person would have all they
had when they ascended.  That would allow for tournament games.  

That gives me an idea for a multi-player game:  have each player control
thier character in a gladiator match, but it doesn't happen in real-time
like I discussed above, but rather each person gets a chance to move in
turn.  By the end of the first couple of rounds, I would expect much of
people's equiptment to be destroyed by fireballs and the like.

